  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Friday)\nIssued at 102 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nBig changes are on the way to the area tonight. An area of low \npressure tracking northeast west of the CWA will be the big \nsource of our big weather changes.\n\nStrong southwest winds are in place over the area today, bringing\nwell above normal afternoon temps. A Red Flag Warning is in place\nin NE WY and NW SD through this evening. Campbell County has a\nHigh Wind Warning in effect until 6 PM MDT due to gusts over 60 \nmph. Winds will diminish this evening.\n\nAs the previously mentioned low pressure tracks east through \nsouthern Canada, a strong cold front will push through tonight. \nThis front will swing winds to the northwest and increase speeds. \nSustained speeds around 25 to 35 with gusts around 35 to 50 mph. A\nWind Advisory has been posted for the zones that will likely see \nthe strongest gusts around 45 to 55 mph. This Advisory will go \ninto effect tonight at Midnight and expire at 9 AM Saturday. \nSaturday will still see gusty winds, but at this time, not to the \nlevel of needing the Advisory.\n\nTemperatures will also be greatly impacted by this front, highs\nthis weekend into next week will be in the 40s and 50s and\novernight lows will be in the 20s and 30s.\n\nAs far as precip goes, as the front pushes through tonight, there\nis a slight chance for rain showers for parts of western SD. Then\nSaturday is looking dry and sunny. But Saturday night through\nMonday, a lingering upper level trough to the west will give the\narea surges of moisture that will be mostly rain but we can't rule\nout snow mixing Sunday morning and again Sunday night into Monday\nmorning.\n\nNext week looks to continue the cooler, near normal, temps with\nthe occasional, short-lived, chances for showers.",
